<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sviatoslav Vsevolodovich</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1196–1252</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sviatoslav-i-of-kiev">Sviatoslav</a> Vsevolodovich (1196–1252) was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vsevolod-the-big-nest">Vsevolod the Big Nest</a> of Vladimir-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suzdal">Suzdal</a> and prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuryev-polsky">Yuryev-Polsky</a>. He built the richly carved white-stone Cathedral of St George there in the 1230s. After the death of his brother Yaroslav he was Grand Prince of Vladimir from 1246 until he was ousted by his nephew Mikhail in 1248.</p></div>
